msgid "Mission Planner Flight Data Screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:7
#: f1023fc9591d4f95b3bce07e554fd36a
msgid "This section covers the information you will need to use the features in the Mission Planner Flight DATA screen - selected in the Top menu of Mission Planner. :ref:`An Introduction <mission-planner-ground-control-station>` provides a brief overview with pointers to the various areas of information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:12
#: 27943b07e7174c57a59b4c5faa0759cd
msgid "Heads Up Area  (HUD)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:13
#: 5e0aef5546e049529321ee542c68d4dc
msgid "This is the area in the upper left corner of the Mission Planner Data screen. Details of what each item is can be found :ref:`here<mission-planner-ground-control-station>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:15
#: bca040b8e4dc442fad90009903a72712
msgid "You can detach the HUD to a separate window by double clicking anywhere in the window. Close the window to put it back in the main Mission Planner window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:18
#: b88bc25c8e4c4daf80688f0ceefb119f
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:19
#: 1eadb530d7384e9bbf933515f5c952e3
msgid "Several Options are available by right-clicking the HUD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:23
#: 335bef412f564f70ac267afd4ad3869b
msgid "Video:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:24
#: 549d22c7609249bc9212d2d5f42039dc
msgid "You can start or stop recording the HUD as an .avi video stored in the logs folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:25
#: 8105a18f01b44a568c422a0e3fbe1e07
msgid "Set MJPEG Source: Connect and display MJPEG video source from the network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:26
#: eded65eac23e49e3837728282e780f58
msgid "Start Camera: If a video source has been selected in the CONFIG/Planner page, start displaying it in the HUD window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:27
#: 875257ed66fe4335b92ec44f3a227c02
msgid "Set GStreamer Source: Connect and display Gstreamer video stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:28
#: f121014daf734708b0b273ec807571cc
msgid "HereLink Video: Display HereLink video, use the same IP as when connecting MP via UDPCL to Herelink for telemetry. See Herelink documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:29
#: 5b7a2a9a77294059bf83d8d4ef54e78b
msgid "GStreamer Stop: Stop GStreamer video."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:31
#: 62363309ddee4219a7b11d8b476824d6
msgid "In the CONFIG/Planner screen, you can select to display video from a capture source on the PC in the HUD window, and have the HUD display overlaid or not on that video."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:33
#: 6755cf91ba7248988ed55069aa04a369
msgid "Set Aspect Ratio: clicking this alternates between 4:1 and 16:9 aspect ratio."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:34
#: fb2f918c6dd14855b155d0e3a5b3ccaf
msgid "User Items: You can add any of the telemetry parameters to the display by right-clicking on the HUD, clicking User Items, and checking the items you want to display. Note that you can also view all of the telemetry in the Control and Status area by clicking the Status button. If Scripting is sending NAMED_VALUE_FLOAT values, these will also appear as an item that you can display in the HUD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:35
#: 6902b260adf141328cd8f5757b408ab9
msgid "Russian HUD: Toggle to/from a Russian style HUD (i.e. ground horizon fixed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:36
#: deafd2c47a714f77a779e585cad7197d
msgid "Swap with Map: swap map to this window and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:37
#: a0777e6787cd41278faa10bb65567f4f
msgid "Ground Color: Click to change the ground color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:38
#: eb80a9febb1b41b198ff9295743c4ef8
msgid "HUD Items: Toggle which items are displaying on the HUD such as heading, speed, altitude, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:39
#: 4df5afb409a64906b0369af30f4a5ab1
msgid "Show icons/text: Toggle between using icons or text for the lower HUD items such as battery capacity, EKF status, VIBE status, and GPS status."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:42
#: be58ffa476c642ee99647ef86202d289
msgid "Control and Status (Lower Left)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:43
#: ff5b1fc92df44b378f2ca9ec3e01388a
msgid "The Control and Status area of the Flight Data screen is in the lower left-hand portion of Mission Planner. In this area, you can select any of several different tabs. Some tabs provide information (e.g. Status) and other items allow control of the vehicle (e.g. Actions) using the telemetry uplink. (Telemetry radio connection is required)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:45
#: a92f4e95ed634a20b308f9bf6a273796
msgid "Quick:  This allows a quick look at just a few telemetry values in large text.  Double-click to add items. Right-click to change the number of rows/columns and move the tab to a separate window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:46
#: 6b5ea4e8b26140a7ac82d6dd6fe91120
msgid "Actions: Use this area to control your Auto Pilot either for testing (using USB and no motor battery) or for controlling your vehicle. You can switch modes, arm/disarm (while on the ground), enable an attached joystick, restart a mission in the air, control a camera mount, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:47
#: 70aeeb1fc0f442c39ba5e826c9d2b153
msgid "The dropdown menus on the left are for (in order from top to bottom) choosing a MAVLink action, choosing a waypoint to set, choosing a mode to set, and choosing the state of the camera mount. The buttons directly to the right of each dropdown send the selected action to the connected vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:48
#: bf59568372c7440a968a8555e972d28b
msgid "There are shortcut buttons for Auto, Loiter, and RTL modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:49
#: e5dbb51ca1814ed6a1368854f130976b
msgid "Joystick: Allows the user to set up a joystick attached to the ground station. See :ref:`common-joystick` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:50
#: 86d1d2bddc004e43b62ac4f53665b182
msgid "Set Home Alt: Set current altitude to zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:51
#: fbe9ee59668f4b13b477cdc14e93d7a1
msgid "Restart Mission: Set the current waypoint to the start of the current mission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:52
#: 2f98877064e64fe5a81b739ca080c6e7
msgid "Raw Sensor View: Shows roll, pitch, and yaw angles. Also shows gyro, accelerometer, 8 RC input channels, and 8 servo output channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:53
#: 12d7c686f52c46c9afcbf65a1dadd03c
msgid "Arm/Disarm: Arm and disarm the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:54
#: 8276b91fc63145d3be893080ebf2eff0
msgid "Resume Mission: Change to Auto mode at the previous waypoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:55
#: aed4feb1668c4c2da350aefab689e804
msgid "Change Speed: This value is always in m/s and performs a DO_CHANGE_SPEED command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:56
#: 559d8b61f2f041a0ab2b62f778a14236
msgid "Change Alt: This value is in the user-selected altitude units. The default units are meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:57
#: ff5d82182fac4376b05e16a3288ec2cd
msgid "Set Loiter Rad: This changes the loiter radius when in Loiter mode in meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:58
#: 14264cedfc034ffcb6613ef12f3f408c
msgid "Clear Track: Clears the purple track line shown on the map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:59
#: 25ee649c94af4915b6fa7bf02e1662c9
msgid "Abort Landing: Commands the vehicle-specific abort landing procedure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:60
#: 19f1a8cded2c459282c97bd5e2b7e780
msgid "Messages: Messages from the vehicle that can range in importance from informational to critical. Important messages also appear on the HUD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:61
#: 25c97597cb6e41e5821824320d4df881
msgid "Gauges: This shows four popular telemetry gauges. Double click the speed gauge to change the top speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:62
#: 8f1801ff24eb436c9d5187c5da605c2a
msgid "Status: Clicking the Status menu button will display all of the telemetry parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:63
#: cf038790d3594a98aa25cd401889b6cb
msgid "Servos/Relay: This allows the setting of any relay pins or setting/overriding RC values for channels 5 thru 14. (Use servo settings with caution, you could change flight modes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:64
#: e8245e4c9b824f63b1e3e7dfacc84c89
msgid ":ref:`Telemetry Logs <planner:mission-planner-telemetry-logs>`:  Use this section to view, analyze, convert, and playback telemetry logs that are recorded by Mission Planner. See :ref:`Playing Back Missions with Tlogs <common-recording-and-playing-back-missions>` for specifics on playing back your mission and viewing the mission in the map area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:65
#: 064b3691909949f2a90968e1e29c1348
msgid "Data Flash Logs:  This provides a means to download data flash logs, analyze them, or create KML/gpx files from them. Click Review a Log to open a log file and establish a new window to view/analyze the log. Details :ref:`here <common-downloading-and-analyzing-data-logs-in-mission-planner>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:66
#: 7e5e8d95576f4e4ebaeae23d9d2e217a
msgid ":ref:`Scripts: <using-python-scripts-in-mission-planner>`: Automation using Python scripts and vehicle state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:68
#: 59e39dfc4114414ab0ef475948c0b92d
msgid "the ability to change modes from the ground station can be restricted, by mode, using the :ref:`FLTMODE_GCSBLOCK<FLTMODE_GCSBLOCK>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:71
#: 11aad9ae18dc4b3fa635764142b16c96
msgid "Map Area"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:72
#: 0b1b65293bdb4146a25ce5ba96bd4d4c
msgid "The map area on the right side of the Flight Data screen displays the vehicle track as it moves, provides other information, and allows the user to enter some control actions - which send commands to the vehicle (telemetry required)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:74
#: 49b5c79ae20c4b838d5f16ade8abd7ac
msgid "Right-click on the map area to select one of these options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:79
#: b0f888077ac94c61bc0c61582a854a0f
msgid "Fly to here: (Command) This is guided mode  (see bottom of this page :ref:`Guided Mode <mission-planner-ground-control-station>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:80
#: c9509500eb2341c48ac11a00f4f9586e
msgid "Fly to here Alt:  (Command) Lets you enter an altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:81
#: dbbfa850d00c4153875b5d8140f84df3
msgid "Fly to Coords: (Command) Lets you fly to a latitude and longitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:82
#: 12dfc8e404cd43d1bceb01826367ef78
msgid "Add POI: Lets you set, delete, save, and load Points of Interest to display on the map"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:83
#: 522deaa3ff03486591d05da4e97348ea
msgid "Point Camera Here: (Command) Points vehicle and camera at the location of the cursor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:84
#: 3165f911a6924141bb515f47d4897723
msgid "Point Camera Coords: (Command) Point vehicle and camera at a location using latitude and longitude coordinates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:85
#: f4d65f183d3845ef9fbd72a7dd21a619
msgid "Trigger Camera Now  (Command): Triggers camera if :ref:`setup <common-camera-shutter-with-servo>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:86
#: 4837eba285de4edb8c180b90f41ab02c
msgid "Flight Planner:  You can open the flight planner window in the map window area and leave the rest of the Flight Data Screen as is. Click the \"CLOSE\" button at top to return."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:87
#: 91b64b2183d1483294fbe5a09492e212
msgid "Set Home Here: (Command) Set new HOME position for RTL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:88
#: 8036d629ade743ad9208194d107aa63c
msgid "TakeOff: (Command) Takeoff and loiter at input altitude. Copter and QuadPlane only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:89
#: 9eaceb05ea89402f82f33f970e6b6bf0
msgid "Camera Overlap: If checked will show camera overlaps on the map during a survey mission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:90
#: 47b1c6935dfc46c0858c915201b5dc4e
msgid "Altitude Angel Settings: Allows reporting and connection to `Altitude Angel services <https://www.altitudeangel.com/>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:91
#: 791823288c69482aadb2b9b8f1506ee3
msgid "Stats : (in development)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:94
#: b970a13f3058458ab3c3fc2c2bdb50e9
msgid "Information/options at the bottom of the map"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:95
#: d9cded12e3a943f8a42f4425adef6fb9
msgid "hdop, sats: shows information about the GPS reception quality and the number of satellites in view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:96
#: ba963e9152a242298e2fc66e1ddd4c97
msgid "Legend:  Each color corresponds to the color of the corresponding line showing directions and headings. Black is the GPS track as your vehicle travels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:97
#: 2885677423ab4927a6438c80a79c8e7d
msgid "Tuning:  Opens/closes the tuning window. Any value in the Status list (double click) can be graphed in real-time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:98
#: 548045cb58b141e4b70c57848e479662
msgid "Auto Pan: Checking this box will make the map follow the vehicle and thus keep the vehicle in the center of the screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:99
#: db775b8c849e48389701752d289a3ffe
msgid "Zoom: Shows or selects the current zoom level of the map. You can also use the:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-data.rst:100
#: 01401c53439349d1a9fd2984d7310b9b
msgid "Scroll bar: Use the scroll bar to change the zoom level of the map."
msgstr ""
